  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1125 PM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nLow clouds and fog are expected across our eastern zones through \nlate morning with clear skies elsewhere. Some high clouds are \nexpected to move into our western zones this afternoon and spread \neastward overnight. Another round of fog is possible tonight with \nprobabilities exceeding 40 percent. Clear skies are then expected \nthrough tomorrow. Winds will be light throughout this period but a \nsoutherly direction. As for temperatures, lows this morning will dip \ninto the 30s with around freezing across our western zones. Highs \ntoday will reach into the mid to upper 50s with lows tonight in the \nmid 30s. Highs tomorrow look to reach into the 60s with lows \ntomorrow night around 40 degrees. Dry conditions continue throughout \nthe remainder of the forecast with high pressure being the dominate \nfeature at the surface. There may be a dry cold front that moves \nthrough the area mid week but future model runs will need to be \nwatched. Highs during this period will reach into the mid 60s to \naround 70 degrees with lows in the upper 30s to upper 40s.",
